    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d217">

                <pb facs="0283" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.731/116: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >House</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-22T12:00:00+00:00"
                            >November 22, 1918—12 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 22—9:03 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>146. Referring further to our number 137.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d217-f1"/> I am
                    now advised by the press correspondents that their messages to the United States
                    are being permitted to pass through without interference by the French
                    censor.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
